 "result": "`jsonify` is defined at `src/tessel/json/__init__.py:138`. It is a thin wrapper that calls `active_app.json.response(*args, **kwargs)` (line 170), so it needs an active app context.\n\n**What it calls internally**\n\n- `active_app.json` is the app's JSON provider. The default implementation is `DefaultJSONProvider` in `src/tessel/json/provider.py`.\n- `response()` (`provider.py:189`) does the work:\n  - `_prepare_response_obj(args, kwargs)` turns positional args into a single value or list, and kwargs into a dict. It rejects both together.\n  - It indents with 2 spaces if `compact` is `False`, or if `compact` is `None` and the app is in debug mode. Otherwise it uses compact separators `(\",\", \":\")`.\n  - It serialises with `self.dumps(obj, **dump_args)`, which wraps `json.dumps`.\n  - It returns `app.response_class(f\"{...}\\n\", mimetype=self.mimetype)`.\n\nBecause it goes through `app.json`, an app can override the behaviour by supplying its own provider. There's also an abstract `response` at `provider.py:89` on the base `JSONProvider`.",
